ell. There was some REALLY good stuff with the &quot;Maybe you're wrong at being angry at God for the world falling,... Maybe God caught the world as it fell and holds it cupped in the palm of his hand...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T06:51:11-08:00","id":1046750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1046580#post1046580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That moment definitely stood out. Some of the things with the Reaper as well. There was some REALLY good stuff with the &quot;Maybe you're wrong at being angry at God for the world falling,... Maybe God caught the world as it fell and holds it cupped in the palm of his hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>It really hammers in the main point of the story is having faith","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T09:06:36-08:00","id":1046805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1046750#post1046750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really hammers in the main point of the story is having faith</div> </div> </div> </div>Or stealing it through deceit because some degree of pissy-ness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T10:35:00-08:00","id":1046837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1046805#post1046805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or stealing it through deceit because some degree of pissy-ness...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. 'i'm gonna say it right away, i don't really liked Gaviel as a Person. Loved him as character, but his arrogance and smamyness really got to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T04:06:22-08:00","id":1048162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1046020#post1046020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know the genius in that part? Is that that vampire just found someone who can confirm one of the greatest mysteries of vampire existence Caine's history, that vampire was meeting someone who could tell him the answer of a question that vampires have been wondering for ten thousand years. And yet that vampire treats it like just something that is cool but not amazing at all. his 100% non chanlant about the whole thing, like it's just tuesday for him</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Noddist could just sit down and have a talk with one of the Fallen they could learn quite a bit. Of course, as per <i>Dies Ignis</i> the First City came after the Fallen getting cast into the Abyss, but it would still inform them of the early years of their progenitor. Hell, there even were Fallen eyewitnesses to the First Murder, so that'd be even more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T05:06:23-08:00","id":1048186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1048162#post1048162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Noddist could just sit down and have a talk with one of the Fallen they could learn quite a bit. Of course, as per <i>Dies Ignis</i> the First City came after the Fallen getting cast into the Abyss, but it would still inform them of the early years of their progenitor. Hell, there even were Fallen eyewitnesses to the First Murder, so that'd be even more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, imagine what a plot twist it would be a Fallen revealed Caine's punishment was not vampirism and they never saw an vampire before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:23:55-08:00","id":1048274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1048186#post1048186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, imagine what a plot twist it would be a Fallen revealed Caine's punishment was not vampirism and they never saw an vampire before!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on, I misremember: Enoch actually PREDATES the Fallen being locked away (D:TF p.50-51). This means that the Antediluvians were around when the Fallen were. Which can raise all sorts of implications regarding the things that went on there and the things that came from there... oh, and do you know what the symbol of the Baali looks like? It's an inverted version of Lucifer's symbol. And their Infernalism... maybe it has to do with keeping the Abyss closed shut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:42:31-08:00","id":1048287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1048274#post1048274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold on, I misremember: Enoch actually PREDATES the Fallen being locked away (D:TF p.50-51). This means that the Antediluvians were around when the Fallen were. Which can raise all sorts of implications regarding the things that went on there and the things that came from there... oh, and do you know what the symbol of the Baali looks like? It's an inverted version of Lucifer's symbol. And their Infernalism... maybe it has to do with keeping the Abyss closed shut?</div> </div> </div> </div>And the demons who are summoned by dark thaumathurgy were actually created by the fallne to be foot soldiers in the war!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T02:54:40-08:00","id":1056028,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the series - half because I think Greg Stolze is very good at telling stories through very fleshed out and dimensional characters, and also because reading the books helped me &quot;get&quot; the game as a whole. Before the series, I never felt like I understood the dynamic of how the memories of the host and the Fallen interact and merge on a mental level. Prior to this, I almost read it like the Psyche/Shadow interactions in Wraith instead of the Fallen being guided by the Earthly experiences.<br /> <br /> And of course afterwards, the obsessive in me made stats for it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Observe obstacles carefully. With ingenuity, they can become levers.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The frailty of genius is that it requires an audience.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12941-blialcain","name":"BlialCain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:25:34-08:00","id":1056126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlialCain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1042382-greg-stolze-s-trilogy-of-the-fallen?p=1056028#post1056028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoyed the series - half because I think Greg Stolze is very good at telling stories through very fleshed out and dimensional characters, and also because reading the books helped me &quot;get&quot; the game as a whole. Before the series, I never felt like I understood the dynamic of how the memories of the host and the Fallen interact and merge on a mental level. Prior to this, I almost read it like the Psyche/Shadow interactions in Wraith instead of the Fallen being guided by the Earthly experiences.<br /> <br /> And of course afterwards, the obsessive in me made stats for it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohmi that's amazing! Yeah the characters felt very real, either very loveable or vry hateable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}